        "source": "claude",
        "summary": "The Strait of Hormuz continues to operate under severe strain. Port arrivals across the Hormuz-area ports, covering both the Persian Gulf and Gulf of Oman sides, reached 739 in the most recent 24 hours, while PortWatch's most recent published day (2026-07-23) recorded 10 transits against a pre-crisis baseline of 88 per day; these figures use different methodologies and cannot be directly compared. At 11:52 UTC, 352 vessels were holding position away from berth, a metric that excludes ships within 25 km of a working port. The Crisis Pressure index remains in the extreme band, with physical transit deviation as its top contributor. The Escalation Forecast index sits in the elevated band and is easing, with the Brent-WTI forward spread cited as the top contributor; that divergence between a static extreme state and a softening forecast is the sharpest editorial signal in today's data. Brent is quoted at $87.93, unchanged since the 2026-08-01 brief, with futures markets closed; no cause for that level is attributed here. On the political track, multiple unverified single-source outlets report that Trump is pausing further Iran strikes pending a potential deal; separately, Iranian state media claims Israeli forces killed 8 more Palestinians including 2 children despite a ceasefire roadmap, which Tehran state media has not independently confirmed. Twenty-five indexed events were recorded in the past 24 hours.",
